---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import Button from "../components/ui/Button.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
    title="Privacy Policy — Never Sleep"
    description="How Never Sleep handles permissions, local settings, and Google AdMob advertising."
>
    <article class="doc">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="lede">Last updated: October 20, 2026</p>
        <div class="actions doc-actions">
            <Button href="/">Back to home</Button>
        </div>

        <div class="doc__body">
            <section>
                <h2>Overview</h2>
                <p>
                    Never Sleep is an Android utility that changes your device screen-off timeout when you
                    explicitly enable the feature. Lizz Studio develops and provides the app. Contact us
                    at <a href="mailto:home@lizz.com">home@lizz.com</a> about this policy or your data.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>Information we process</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Screen timeout setting</strong> — When you turn Never Sleep on, the app
                        writes a higher value to Android’s system screen-off timeout and stores your
                        previous timeout locally so it can be restored.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>App preferences</strong> — The previous timeout, current mode, and ads
                        preference are stored in the app’s private storage. The app does not send these
                        settings to Lizz Studio. Android cloud backup and device transfer are disabled
                        for the app’s stored data.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Advertising data</strong> — If you leave ads enabled and the applicable
                        consent flow permits ad requests, the Google Mobile Ads SDK may automatically
                        collect and share your IP address (which may be used to estimate general location),
                        app and ad interactions, diagnostic information, and device or account identifiers,
                        including the Android advertising ID and app set ID.
                        Google uses this information for advertising, analytics, and fraud prevention. See
                        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s Privacy Policy</a>
                        and
                        <a href="https://developers.google.com/admob/android/privacy/play-data-disclosure"
                            >Google Mobile Ads data disclosure</a
                        >.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>What we do not do</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>The app has no user accounts and does not request names, emails, or contacts.</li>
                    <li>We do not sell your personal information.</li>
                    <li>
                        We do not upload your screen-timeout preference to our servers — it stays on your
                        device. If you email support, we receive the information you choose to send,
                        including your email address, to respond to your request.
                    </li>
                    <li>We do not request your precise location, contacts, photos, or files.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>Permissions</h2>
                <p>
                    <strong>Modify system settings</strong> — Required for the core feature. You grant this
                    manually in Android Settings → Apps → Special app access.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong>Internet &amp; network state</strong> — Used to refresh the privacy choices
                    required for Google advertising and, when banner ads are enabled, to load ads. You can
                    disable ad requests in the in-app Settings menu.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>Security and sharing</h2>
                <p>
                    Android’s app sandbox protects the app’s local preferences. Google Mobile Ads
                    encrypts the data it collects in transit using TLS. Advertising and consent data
                    are processed by Google under its policies; the app does not send your screen-timeout
                    setting to Google. Lizz Studio does not operate an analytics or account server for
                    this app. No storage or transmission system can be guaranteed completely secure.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
                <p>
                    Local preferences remain until you clear the app’s storage in Android Settings or
                    uninstall it. Turn Never Sleep off first so it can restore your previous timeout:
                    clearing storage or uninstalling while it is enabled may leave the system timeout
                    unchanged. You can also set your preferred timeout in Android’s display settings.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Google controls the retention of advertising and consent data it processes. See
                    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/retention">Google’s retention policy</a>
                    and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">privacy controls</a>. Turning ads
                    off stops new banner ad requests; it does not delete data already held by Google.
                    Android’s privacy settings let you reset or delete your advertising ID.
                </p>
                <p>
                    We retain support correspondence for as long as needed to address your inquiry,
                    meet legal obligations, or handle an ongoing dispute. You can request deletion by emailing
                    <a href="mailto:home@lizz.com">home@lizz.com</a>. We will explain any information
                    we must retain. There is no in-app account to delete.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>Your choices</h2>
                <p>
                    You can turn ads off at any time in Never Sleep → Settings. Where required, Settings
                    also includes Privacy choices so you can review or change the consent choices presented
                    by Google. You can review or revoke Modify system settings access in Android Settings
                    without uninstalling the app. Turn Never Sleep off before revoking access if you
                    want it to restore your previous timeout. Where applicable, you may contact us to
                    request access, correction, or deletion of information you have provided to us, or
                    raise a concern with your local data protection authority.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>Website campaign links</h2>
                <p>
                    Links to Google Play can include a public source and campaign label, such as
                    the name of a video campaign. Google Play uses these labels in its acquisition
                    reports. We do not add a personal identifier to these links or use cookies or
                    local storage for campaign attribution on this website.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>Children</h2>
                <p>
                    Never Sleep is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal
                    information from children.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>Changes</h2>
                <p>
                    We may update this policy. The “Last updated” date at the top will change when we do.
                    Any consent required for a new use of data will be requested separately.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>Contact</h2>
                <p>
                    Lizz Studio — <a href="mailto:home@lizz.com">home@lizz.com</a>.
                    For non-private bug reports, you can also use the
                    <a href="https://github.com/Lizzergas/never-sleep/issues">project’s issue tracker</a>.
                    GitHub issues are public; please email us for personal or sensitive inquiries.
                </p>
            </section>
        </div>
    </article>
</SiteLayout>
